# Join social + love: a marriage profile is two Condorcet profiles, one per side. Read-only on culture/love (its check writes a file there, so it is not run here).
check "python3 -I culture/social/condorcet.py"
seq profiles = from culture/love/fingerprints.json "preference profiles"
claim formula profiles = "((n!)**n)**2" from 1
claim profiles = [1, 16, 46656]
frame "Join: preference profiles of culture/love (n + n people, each ranks the other side) and Condorcet profiles of culture/social (voters rank options)" reading "one side of a love profile is n voters ranking n options, a Condorcet profile, so love counts ((n!)^n)^2: 1, 16, 46656; at n = 3 that is 216^2, with 216 the profile count condorcet.py asserts" -> 4 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
record culture/social join-love checked-finite "core/ontology/joins/social_love.ath: the stored preference profiles of culture/love (1, 16, 46656 for n = 1..3) equal ((n!)^n)^2, two Condorcet profiles of n voters on n options, one per side; at n = 3 this is 216^2, and culture/social/condorcet.py, which asserts the 216, passes in the same run. culture/love/check.py is not run here (it writes beside itself)."
